      "content": "thanks. the \"official narrative\" approach makes sense. it's just that some of these \"distractions\" are getting pretty obvious. like, last night the mayor was talking about the new downtown park project for twenty minutes, but then there was that sudden surge in power grid maintenance reports right after. it's almost too convenient. if i'm in a setting where someone might notice me connecting those dots, how do i redirect the conversation if someone asks why i'm being so quiet or why i'm looking at the grid reports instead of the park news?",
